# Git for Windows ships core.autocrlf=true in its system config, so without
# attributes every shell script here checked out CRLF and bash died on
# `set -euo pipefail\r` (test_legacy_release_mutators_fail_closed went red on
# a clean tree). All 67 tracked files are already LF in the index, so these
# lines change no blob and cannot affect the Linux runner; an existing Windows
# worktree only picks them up on the next checkout of the file.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
